,"tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#hook--native-modules","content":"Filename convention:","locale":"en"},"1698":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#hook--native-modules","content":"Load search paths:","locale":"en"},"1699":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#hook--native-modules","content":"Native addon API:","locale":"en"},"1700":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#hook--native-modules","content":"**`getAllMainProcess`** — enumerate QQ main processes.","locale":"en"},"1701":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#hook--native-modules","content":"**`loadModuleManual`** — manually map the injection module into the target process.","locale":"en"},"1702":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#hook--native-modules","content":"**`unloadModuleManual`** — unload an injected module.","locale":"en"},"1703":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#hook--native-modules","content":"Default target process is `QQ.exe` on Windows, `qq` on Linux.","locale":"en"},"1704":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-27","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#onebot-lifecycle","content":"When the bridge detects a QQ session starting:","locale":"en"},"1705":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-28","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#onebot-lifecycle","content":"Load `config/onebot_<uin>.json` (or copy from global if missing).","locale":"en"},"1706":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-29","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#onebot-lifecycle","content":"Construct `OneBotInstance`.","locale":"en"},"1707":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-30","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#onebot-lifecycle","content":"Boot HTTP / WS / reverse WS / HTTP-POST adapters per `networks.*` config.","locale":"en"},"1708":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-31","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#onebot-lifecycle","content":"Asynchronously warm up the friend list, group list, and group members.","locale":"en"},"1709":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-32","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#onebot-lifecycle","content":"Forward bridge events into OneBot events.","locale":"en"},"1710":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-33","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#onebot-lifecycle","content":"When the session closes the matching instance is released.","locale":"en"},"1711":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-34","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#websocket-package","content":"`@snowluma/websocket` is the in-repo WebSocket implementation; its surface tracks `ws` closely while routing through a native fast path.","locale":"en"},"1712":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-35","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#websocket-package","content":"Exports:","locale":"en"},"1713":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-36","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#websocket-package","content":"**`WebSocket`** — client constructor.","locale":"en"},"1714":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-37","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#websocket-package","content":"**`WebSocketServer`** — server constructor.","locale":"en"},"1715":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-38","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#websocket-package","content":"**`Server`** — alias for `WebSocketServer`.","locale":"en"},"1716":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-39","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#websocket-package","content":"**`InternalWebSocket`** — internal connection implementation.","locale":"en"},"1717":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-40","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#websocket-package","content":"Loads its own platform-specific `.node` from the same `native/` search paths.","locale":"en"},"1718":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-41","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#sdk-package","content":"`@snowluma/sdk` is a typed OneBot client for downstream consumers — standalone-publishable to npm and independent of the SnowLuma runtime. It's built inside the monorepo (see `pnpm build:sdk` / `build:all` below); for consumer-side usage see the SDK docs.","locale":"en"},"1719":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-42","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#build-order","content":"Full distribution:","locale":"en"},"1720":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-43","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#build-order","content":"Runs, in order:","locale":"en"},"1721":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-44","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#build-order","content":"`@snowluma/core` full build","locale":"en"},"1722":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-45","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#build-order","content":"`@snowluma/sdk`","locale":"en"},"1723":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-46","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#build-order","content":"`webui`","locale":"en"},"1724":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-47","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#build-order","content":"Output goes to the repo root `dist/`.","locale":"en"},"1725":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-48","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#docs-site","content":"The docs site lives in a separate repo: `SnowLuma/SnowLumaDocs`. Local development usually checks it out at `dev/SnowLumaDocs/` alongside SnowLuma.","locale":"en"},"1726":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-49","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#docs-site","content":"Stack: Rspress + React + TypeScript + MDX + KaTeX.","locale":"en"},"1727":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-50","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#docs-site","content":"The OneBot API reference is generated by the docs repo's `pnpm api:generate` (also wired to `prebuild`) from `docs/public/api/catalog.json` — one page per action, plus a category overview and a searchable landing page. `catalog.json` is the action catalog produced by the main repo's `collectActionDocs()` (same shape as `@snowluma/mcp`'s `CatalogAction`); the main repo's `sync-docs-catalog` workflow commits it here automatically via the SnowLuma bot on release — no manual upkeep.","locale":"en"},"1728":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-51","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#contribution-notes","content":"**Don't bypass `BridgeManager`** — every OneBot action should reach NTQQ through `BridgeInterface`. Keeps the OneBot layer decoupled and testable.","locale":"en"},"1729":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-52","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#contribution-notes","content":"**Keep configs auto-generatable** — new fields must stay backwards-compatible; normalize them on load and write the result back.","locale":"en"},"1730":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-53","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#contribution-notes","content":"**Native modules are per-platform** — when adding a platform, sync the `.node` and the injectable library.","locale":"en"},"1731":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-54","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#contribution-notes","content":"**Tests first** — core OneBot behavior should be validated with `vitest`; see `packages/core/tests/`.","locale":"en"},"1732":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-55","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#contribution-notes","content":"**API docs automation** — just add the action with `defineAction` (optionally `returnsSchema` to describe `data`); `catalog.json` is kept in sync by the `sync-docs-catalog` workflow, so the API reference never drifts. Run `pnpm api:generate` locally to preview.","locale":"en"},"1733":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","type":"page","content":"Troubleshooting","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/faq","locale":"en"},"1734":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/faq","content":"QR login, passwords, ports, injection, and image pulls","locale":"en"},"1735":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#novnc-never-connects--spins-forever","content":"noVNC never connects / spins forever","locale":"en"},"1736":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#cannot-find-the-webui-password","content":"Cannot find the WebUI password","locale":"en"},"1737":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#a-bot-cannot-reach-3000--3001","content":"A bot cannot reach 3000 / 3001","locale":"en"},"1738":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#injection-fails--qq-runs-but-never-comes-online","content":"Injection fails / QQ runs but never comes online","locale":"en"},"1739":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#image-pull-hangs-in-china","content":"Image pull hangs in China","locale":"en"},"1740":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#upgrade-asks-you-to-scan-again","content":"Upgrade asks you to scan again","locale":"en"},"1741":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#novnc-never-connects--spins-forever","content":"Confirm port `6081` is published. Official templates **do not** publish `5900`.","locale":"en"},"1742":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#novnc-never-connects--spins-forever","content":"There is **no** shared default remote-desktop password. The first start generates a random one and prints it once; later restarts will not print it again — use the value you saved.","locale":"en"},"1743":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#novnc-never-connects--spins-forever","content":"High CPU and no handshake: pass `--ulimit nofile=65536:1048576` (already in official compose).","locale":"en"},"1744":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#cannot-find-the-webui-password","content":"The bootstrap password is printed only on the **first start of a fresh data volume**. Reusing a volume will not print a new one.","locale":"en"},"1745":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#a-bot-cannot-reach-3000--3001","content":"In Docker, OneBot should listen on `0.0.0.0`. Upgrading the image rewrites a leftover loopback default; a host you set yourself is left alone.","locale":"en"},"1746":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#a-bot-cannot-reach-3000--3001","content":"On the compose network use the service name `snowluma`, not `127.0.0.1`.","locale":"en"},"1747":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#a-bot-cannot-reach-3000--3001","content":"Send the access token.","locale":"en"},"1748":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#injection-fails--qq-runs-but-never-comes-online","content":"You still need `SYS_PTRACE` and `seccomp=unconfined`.","locale":"en"},"1749":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#injection-fails--qq-runs-but-never-comes-online","content":"Do not start a second QQ as root inside the container.","locale":"en"},"1750":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#injection-fails--qq-runs-but-never-comes-online","content":"`ptrace_scope=3` refuses ptrace outright.","locale":"en"},"1751":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#injection-fails--qq-runs-but-never-comes-online","content":"Do not delete the `qq-gateway-data`, `qq-client-config`, or `qq-client-data` volumes.","locale":"en"},"1752":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#image-pull-hangs-in-china","content":"That hop is Docker Hub. The installer retries with prefixes. Manually:","locale":"en"},"1753":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#image-pull-hangs-in-china","content":"On 1Panel / Baota, set a registry mirror in the panel. The installer will not rewrite `daemon.json`.","locale":"en"},"1754":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#upgrade-asks-you-to-scan-again","content":"Recreating the container can look like a new device. Keep the volumes. If you still must log in again, scan via noVNC.","locale":"en"},"1755":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","type":"page","content":"Introduction","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","locale":"en"},"1756":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","content":"What SnowLuma is, what you can do with it, and its three usage shapes and release layout","locale":"en"},"1757":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#three-usage-shapes","content":"Three usage shapes","locale":"en"},"1758":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#release-layout","content":"Release layout","locale":"en"},"1759":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#default-services","content":"Default services","locale":"en"},"1760":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#project-status","content":"Project status","locale":"en"},"1761":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#next-steps","content":"Next steps","locale":"en"},"1762":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","content":"SnowLuma is a **remote-protocol framework** for NTQQ (the QQ desktop client). It bridges QQ into the OneBot v11 ecosystem: a native addon injects a hook into the running QQ process via ptrace-class injection (Linux process `qq`, Windows `QQ.exe`), decodes its internal packets, and exposes them as OneBot v11 over HTTP / WebSocket / reverse-WS / HTTP-POST.","locale":"en"},"1763":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","content":"Around that core, SnowLuma also ships:","locale":"en"},"1764":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","content":"**OneBot v11 adapters** — HTTP API server, WebSocket server, reverse WebSocket, and HTTP event reporting, in any combination.","locale":"en"},"1765":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","content":"**NTQQ bridge** — talks to the real QQ client directly; no protocol account, no separate login.","locale":"en"},"1766":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","content":"**Multi-account** — one OneBot instance per UIN, auto-detected and auto-attached, no manual config.","locale":"en"},"1767":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","content":"**Built-in WebUI** — manage accounts, config, and status from the browser.","locale":"en"},"1768":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","content":"**TypeScript SDK** — `@snowluma/sdk`, for writing fully typed OneBot clients.","locale":"en"},"1769":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","content":"**MCP server** — `@snowluma/mcp`, so MCP-capable AI clients can query and invoke OneBot actions.","locale":"en"},"1770":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#three-usage-shapes","content":"Your goal","locale":"en"},"1771":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#three-usage-shapes","content":"Shape","locale":"en"},"1772":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#three-usage-shapes","content":"Start here","locale":"en"},"1773":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#three-usage-shapes","content":"Run a bot long-term on a server","locale":"en"},"1774":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#three-usage-shapes","content":"**Docker** (recommended)","locale":"en"},"1775":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#three-usage-shapes","content":"Docker deployment","locale":"en"},"1776":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#three-usage-shapes","content":"Let an AI client drive QQ","locale":"en"},"1777":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#three-usage-shapes","content":"**MCP**","locale":"en"},"1778":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#three-usage-shapes","content":"MCP integration","locale":"en"},"1779":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#three-usage-shapes","content":"Try it quickly on a local machine","locale":"en"},"1780":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#three-usage-shapes","content":"**Prebuilt tarball**","locale":"en"},"1781":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#three-usage-shapes","content":"Choose a deployment","locale":"en"},"1782":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#three-usage-shapes","content":"To write client code, see the TypeScript SDK.","locale":"en"},"1783":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-27","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#release-layout","content":"Each platform ships two tarball flavors on GitHub Releases:","locale":"en"},"1784":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-28","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#release-layout","content":"Filename","locale":"en"},"1785":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-29","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#release-layout","content":"Bundles Node.js?","locale":"en"},"1786":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-30","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#release-layout","content":"When to use","locale":"en"},"1787":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-31","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#release-layout","content":"`SnowLuma-<TAG>-<platform>-<arch>.tar.gz` (**full**)","locale":"en"},"1788":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-32","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#release-layout","content":"Yes, bundles a Node runtime","locale":"en"},"1789":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-33","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#release-layout","content":"No Node installed; runs out of the box","locale":"en"},"1790":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-34","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#release-layout","content":"`SnowLuma-<TAG>-<platform>-<arch>-lite.tar.gz` (**lite**)","locale":"en"},"1791":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-35","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#release-layout","content":"No (much smaller)","locale":"en"},"1792":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-36","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#release-layout","content":"Node.js ≥ 22 already installed (Node 24 LTS recommended)","locale":"en"},"1793":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-37","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#release-layout","content":"Published platforms / arches: `linux-x64`, `linux-arm64`, `win-x64`.","locale":"en"},"1794":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-38","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#release-layout","content":"SnowLuma requires **Node.js ≥ 22**. As of 2026, **Node 24 (\"Krypton\") is Active LTS** and 22 (\"Jod\") is Maintenance LTS, so for the lite tarball install **Node 24 LTS** (22 still works). The full tarball bundles its own runtime — no install needed. Source: nodejs.org.","locale":"en"},"1795":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-39","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#release-layout","content":"After unpacking, the `dist/` tree looks roughly like:","locale":"en"},"1796":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-40","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#release-layout","content":"To run: unpack, then `node ./index.mjs`. On Windows you can also double-click `launcher.bat`.","locale":"en"},"1797":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-41","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#default-services","content":"Service","locale":"en"},"1798":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-42","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#default-services","content":"Default listen","locale":"en"},"1799":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-43","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#default-services","content":"Notes","locale":"en"},"1800":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-44","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#default-services","content":"OneBot HTTP","locale":"en"},"1801":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-45","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#default-services","content":"`0.0.0.0:3000`","locale":"en"},"1802":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-46","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction"