ontent":"Requires **Node.js ≥ 22** (Node 24 LTS recommended). The package is pure ESM (`\"type\": \"module\"`) and ships its own type declarations.","locale":"en"},"1973":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-16","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#supported-transports","content":"Transport","locale":"en"},"1974":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-17","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#supported-transports","content":"Client class","locale":"en"},"1975":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-18","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#supported-transports","content":"Default endpoint","locale":"en"},"1976":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-19","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#supported-transports","content":"HTTP (POST JSON)","locale":"en"},"1977":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-20","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#supported-transports","content":"`SnowLumaHttpClient`","locale":"en"},"1978":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-21","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#supported-transports","content":"`http://127.0.0.1:3000/`","locale":"en"},"1979":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-22","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#supported-transports","content":"WebSocket (forward / reverse, with events)","locale":"en"},"1980":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-23","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#supported-transports","content":"`SnowLumaWebSocketClient`","locale":"en"},"1981":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-24","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#supported-transports","content":"`ws://127.0.0.1:3001/`","locale":"en"},"1982":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-25","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#supported-transports","content":"Both clients extend the abstract `SnowLumaApiClient` base, so `call()` / `request()` and every camelCase action shortcut work identically across transports. HTTP suits plain request/response scripts; WebSocket adds **realtime event delivery** on top.","locale":"en"},"1983":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-26","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#http","content":"`SnowLumaHttpClientOptions`:","locale":"en"},"1984":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-27","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#http","content":"`baseUrl?` — OneBot HTTP endpoint, defaults to `http://127.0.0.1:3000/`.","locale":"en"},"1985":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-28","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#http","content":"`accessToken?` — token from the OneBot config; when set, an `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header is sent automatically.","locale":"en"},"1986":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-29","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#http","content":"`requestTimeoutMs?` — default timeout in ms, defaults to `30000`.","locale":"en"},"1987":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-30","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#http","content":"`fetch?` — custom `fetch` implementation (tests or non-standard runtimes).","locale":"en"},"1988":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-31","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#http","content":"`headers?` — extra headers attached to every request.","locale":"en"},"1989":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-32","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#websocket","content":"`SnowLumaWebSocketClientOptions`:","locale":"en"},"1990":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-33","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#websocket","content":"`url?` — OneBot WebSocket endpoint, defaults to `ws://127.0.0.1:3001/`.","locale":"en"},"1991":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-34","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#websocket","content":"`accessToken?` — appended to the connection URL as a query parameter.","locale":"en"},"1992":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-35","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#websocket","content":"`requestTimeoutMs?` — default request timeout, defaults to `30000`.","locale":"en"},"1993":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-36","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#websocket","content":"`role?` — role the client advertises: `'Api'` | `'Event'` | `'Universal'` (default `'Universal'`).","locale":"en"},"1994":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-37","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#websocket","content":"`reconnect?` — `true` or a `ReconnectOptions` (`retries` / `minDelayMs` / `maxDelayMs`) to enable auto-reconnect after an unexpected close.","locale":"en"},"1995":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-38","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#websocket","content":"`protocols?` / `webSocket?` — optional subprotocols, optional custom `WebSocket` constructor (Node runtimes or tests).","locale":"en"},"1996":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-39","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#websocket","content":"Browsers and Node 24 ship a global `WebSocket` that works out of the box. To use an implementation like the `ws` package, pass it to the `webSocket` option.","locale":"en"},"1997":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-40","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#websocket","content":"> The factory functions `createHttpClient(options?)` and `createWebSocketClient(options?)` are equivalent to `new`; use whichever you prefer.","locale":"en"},"1998":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-41","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#calling-an-action","content":"Common endpoints have fully typed camelCase methods (`getLoginInfo`, `sendGroupMessage`, `setGroupBan`, …). Any registered action can be called via `raw` / `rawResponse`.","locale":"en"},"1999":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-42","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#calling-an-action","content":"The underlying methods:","locale":"en"},"2000":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-43","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#calling-an-action","content":"`call(action, params?, options?)` — sends the action and returns `data`; throws `SnowLumaApiError` when `status` is `failed` or `retcode !== 0`.","locale":"en"},"2001":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-44","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#calling-an-action","content":"`request(action, params?, options?)` — returns the full response envelope and does not throw on business errors.","locale":"en"},"2002":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-45","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#calling-an-action","content":"Every request can override behavior via `RequestOptions`: `echo` (correlation value), `timeoutMs` (`0` disables the timeout), and `signal` (an `AbortSignal`).","locale":"en"},"2003":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-46","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#subscribing-to-events","content":"Event subscription is a WebSocket-client capability. The client correlates API responses by `echo` and dispatches packets without an `echo` as events.","locale":"en"},"2004":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-47","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#subscribing-to-events","content":"Available event helpers: `onMessage` / `onPrivateMessage` / `onGroupMessage` / `onNotice(type?)` / `onRequest(type?)` / `onMetaEvent` / `command()`, plus the lower-level `onEvent`, `when(predicate, handler)`, and `use(middleware)`. Lifecycle events use `on('open' | 'close' | 'error' | 'response' | 'raw', …)`. Every `on` / `when` / `use` returns an unsubscribe function.","locale":"en"},"2005":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-48","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#subscribing-to-events","content":"The event context (`ctx`) has built-in shortcuts:","locale":"en"},"2006":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-49","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#subscribing-to-events","content":"`ctx.reply(message)` — auto-replies to the private/group thread.","locale":"en"},"2007":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-50","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#subscribing-to-events","content":"`ctx.approve()` / `ctx.reject(reason)` — handle friend or group requests.","locale":"en"},"2008":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-51","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#subscribing-to-events","content":"`ctx.quickOperation(operation)` — calls `.handle_quick_operation`.","locale":"en"},"2009":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-52","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#subscribing-to-events","content":"`ctx.stopPropagation()` — stops further middleware dispatch.","locale":"en"},"2010":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-53","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#message-builder","content":"The SDK ships a chainable message builder and segment factories; send methods accept their output directly:","locale":"en"},"2011":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-54","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#message-builder","content":"Built-in segments: `text`, `br`, `face`, `at`, `atAll`, `reply`, `image`, `record`, `video`, `json`, `xml`, `poke`, `forward`, `node`, `share`, `music`, `location`, `contact`, `raw`. `reply()` may appear only once per chain.","locale":"en"},"2012":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-55","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#auto-reconnect-ack-correlation-and-shared-types","content":"**Ack correlation** — the WebSocket client generates an `echo` per request and routes the response back to the right `Promise`, so concurrent requests never cross. Override the correlation value via `RequestOptions.echo`.","locale":"en"},"2013":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-56","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#auto-reconnect-ack-correlation-and-shared-types","content":"**Auto-reconnect** — `reconnect: true` (or a `ReconnectOptions`) enables exponential backoff (`minDelayMs` defaults to 1000, `maxDelayMs` to 30000). On disconnect, all pending requests reject with `SnowLumaConnectionError`.","locale":"en"},"2014":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-57","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#auto-reconnect-ack-correlation-and-shared-types","content":"**Shared action types** — action names, params, and result types share their source with `@snowluma/core`, so the call surface always matches the server.","locale":"en"},"2015":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-58","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#auto-reconnect-ack-correlation-and-shared-types","content":"**Unified error model** — all errors extend `SnowLumaError`: business failures throw `SnowLumaApiError` (auth-class retcodes become `SnowLumaAuthError`); transport issues throw the `SnowLumaTransportError` subclasses `SnowLumaConnectionError` / `SnowLumaParseError` / `SnowLumaTimeoutError` / `SnowLumaAbortError`.","locale":"en"},"2016":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-59","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#subpath-imports","content":"Beyond the main entry, the package exposes per-module exports: `@snowluma/sdk/client`, `/messages`, `/events`, `/types`, `/errors`, `/actions`. Import only what you need.","locale":"en"},"2017":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-60","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#see-also","content":"Configuration — enable and secure the OneBot HTTP / WS adapters and get an `accessToken`.","locale":"en"},"2018":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-61","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#see-also","content":"Developer guide — monorepo layout and runtime internals.","locale":"en"},"2019":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-62","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#see-also","content":"MCP server — an alternative integration path for LLMs.","locale":"en"},"2020":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/baota","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/baota","type":"page","content":"BT Panel Deploy","breadcrumbs":[