/deploy/docker","content":"This page is the **recommended Linux path**. Image build scripts and Compose templates live in `SnowLuma/SnowLuma.Docker.Framework`. There is also an experimental one-click installer in Alpha — not the default.","locale":"en"},"2070":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#image","content":"Item","locale":"en"},"2071":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#image","content":"Value","locale":"en"},"2072":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#image","content":"Image","locale":"en"},"2073":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#image","content":"`motricseven7/snowluma:latest` (or a specific tag, e.g. `:v1.10.0`)","locale":"en"},"2074":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-27","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#image","content":"Arch","locale":"en"},"2075":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-28","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#image","content":"`linux/amd64`, `linux/arm64`","locale":"en"},"2076":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-29","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#image","content":"Base","locale":"en"},"2077":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-30","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#image","content":"`node:22-bookworm-slim`","locale":"en"},"2078":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-31","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#image","content":"Bundled","locale":"en"},"2079":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-32","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#image","content":"Linux QQ, Xvfb, VNC, noVNC, supervisord, SnowLuma `lite`","locale":"en"},"2080":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-33","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#image","content":"The image does **not** rebuild SnowLuma — it consumes the prebuilt `lite` tarball from each SnowLuma GitHub Release, so the release and the image build are decoupled.","locale":"en"},"2081":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-34","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#ports","content":"Port","locale":"en"},"2082":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-35","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#ports","content":"Purpose","locale":"en"},"2083":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-36","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#ports","content":"`6081`","locale":"en"},"2084":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-37","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#ports","content":"noVNC (browser desktop for QR login)","locale":"en"},"2085":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-38","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#ports","content":"`5099`","locale":"en"},"2086":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-39","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#ports","content":"SnowLuma WebUI","locale":"en"},"2087":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-40","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#ports","content":"`3000`","locale":"en"},"2088":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-41","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#ports","content":"OneBot HTTP (default)","locale":"en"},"2089":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-42","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#ports","content":"`3001`","locale":"en"},"2090":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-43","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#ports","content":"OneBot WebSocket (default)","locale":"en"},"2091":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-44","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#ports","content":"Official templates **publish `6081` only**. They do not map raw VNC `5900`. Add `-p 127.0.0.1:5900:5900` yourself if you need a native VNC client.","locale":"en"},"2092":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-45","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#remote-desktop-password","content":"The official image has **no** public fixed password. Do not copy sample values from old docs or random posts.","locale":"en"},"2093":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-46","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#remote-desktop-password","content":"**Leave `VNC_PASSWD` unset**: the first start generates a random password and **prints it once** in the container logs (one Chinese line, one English line). It is kept on the data volume. Recreating the container or upgrading the image does not change it, as long as the volume is still there, and it will not be printed again.","locale":"en"},"2094":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-47","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#remote-desktop-password","content":"**Set your own password**: pass `VNC_PASSWD` at start. The password is rotated only when you change this value, and the new one is printed once.","locale":"en"},"2095":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-48","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#remote-desktop-password","content":"If the variable still holds the old public default from earlier docs, the next start treats it as unset and replaces it with a new random password.","locale":"en"},"2096":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-49","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#remote-desktop-password","content":"Do not publish `6081` on an untrusted network either.","locale":"en"},"2097":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-50","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#remote-desktop-password","content":"Read the current password (it only appears when generated or when you rotate it):","locale":"en"},"2098":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-51","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#remote-desktop-password","content":"If a later restart no longer shows it, that is expected — use the value you saved the first time.","locale":"en"},"2099":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-52","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#ptrace-permissions","content":"`--cap-add=SYS_PTRACE` and `--security-opt seccomp=unconfined` are still required.","locale":"en"},"2100":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-53","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#ptrace-permissions","content":"SnowLuma's native addon uses `ptrace` to inject the hook into the in-container QQ process. The official image grants `cap_sys_ptrace` to `/usr/local/bin/node`, so SnowLuma can run as the unprivileged `snowluma` user while still injecting within the container's capability boundary.","locale":"en"},"2101":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-54","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#ptrace-permissions","content":"With current official images, you no longer need to change the host's `kernel.yama.ptrace_scope`. Keep these container options instead:","locale":"en"},"2102":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-55","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#ptrace-permissions","content":"To verify the file capability inside the container:","locale":"en"},"2103":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-56","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#ptrace-permissions","content":"If an old image still asks you to relax the host sysctl, upgrade the image first. Changing `kernel.yama.ptrace_scope` should only be a temporary troubleshooting fallback when upgrading is not possible.","locale":"en"},"2104":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-57","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#one-line-docker-run","content":"`--cap-add=SYS_PTRACE` and `--security-opt seccomp=unconfined` are **mandatory**. SnowLuma's native addon uses ptrace to inject the hook into the QQ process; the default seccomp profile blocks that.","locale":"en"},"2105":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-58","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#one-line-docker-run","content":"`--shm-size=1g` is needed for QQ's Chromium runtime — the default container `/dev/shm` is too small and QQ will crash.","locale":"en"},"2106":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker-59","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/docker#docker-compose","content":"Recommended over `docker run`. The repo's `docker-compose.yml`:","locale":"en"},"2107":{"id":