2#route-a-docker-desktops-wsl-integration-recommended","content":"> Official docs: https\\://docs.docker.com/desktop/features/wsl/","locale":"en"},"2602":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2#route-b-native-docker-engine-inside-the-distro","content":"If you'd rather not install Docker Desktop, install native Docker Engine directly inside the Ubuntu distro. For the official apt repo (deb822 `docker.sources` format), see https\\://docs.docker.com/engine/install/ubuntu/.","locale":"en"},"2603":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2#route-b-native-docker-engine-inside-the-distro","content":"For local / dev use only, the convenience script also works:","locale":"en"},"2604":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2#route-b-native-docker-engine-inside-the-distro","content":"After adding yourself to the group you must **reopen the terminal** for it to take effect. Start Docker:","locale":"en"},"2605":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2#route-b-native-docker-engine-inside-the-distro","content":"**Pick Route A or B — don't run both.** Docker Desktop's integration and a native dockerd inside the distro will fight each other if both are present.","locale":"en"},"2606":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2#3-run-the-snowluma-container","content":"With Docker ready, run the exact same command from the canonical Docker page in the Ubuntu terminal:","locale":"en"},"2607":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2#3-run-the-snowluma-container","content":"`--cap-add=SYS_PTRACE` and `--security-opt seccomp=unconfined` are **required** — the hook injects via ptrace, which the default seccomp profile blocks.","locale":"en"},"2608":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2#3-run-the-snowluma-container","content":"The full reference — Compose, env vars, volumes, multi-account, first login — all lives in Docker (Linux) deployment and is not repeated here.","locale":"en"},"2609":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2#4-accessing-ports-from-windows","content":"WSL2 forwards container-listened ports to the Windows `localhost` by default, so you can use `localhost` directly in a Windows browser:","locale":"en"},"2610":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2-27","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2#4-accessing-ports-from-windows","content":"URL","locale":"en"},"2611":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2-28","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2#4-accessing-ports-from-windows","content":"Purpose","locale":"en"},"2612":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2-29","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2#4-accessing-ports-from-windows","content":"`http://localhost:6081/`","locale":"en"},"2613":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2-30","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2#4-accessing-ports-from-windows","content":"noVNC (scan QR for QQ)","locale":"en"},"2614":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2-31","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/wsl2#4-accessing-ports-from-windows","content":"`http://localhost:5099/`","locale":"en"},"2615":{"id":"/en/docs/gu